  "publicationDraft": "Stew cashed in Achane's four-touchdown breakout and Nacua's scorching rookie start for Lamb and Etienne. Kuhl's gamble initially delivered 59.40 points in Week 4, then both acquired backs suffered knee injuries. Nacua kept the package afloat and eventually broke rookie receiving records. Stew flipped Lamb after two starts and Etienne in November, so judging the deal on their full NFL seasons would be misleading. Kuhl beat Stew twice afterward, including a 148.16–125.30 December win with 49.20 from Conner and Nacua. Stew bought proven talent but barely kept it long enough to enjoy it. Kuhl bought the breakout and rode it.",
